From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] services, sechost: failure actions applied, failure-actions flag, SID type, required privileges, launch protection

Service configuration levels that Wine accepted and dropped, or refused.
services.exe now keeps SERVICE_CONFIG_FAILURE_ACTIONS (the FailureActions
binary value of Windows), FAILURE_ACTIONS_FLAG, SERVICE_SID_INFO,
REQUIRED_PRIVILEGES_INFO and LAUNCH_PROTECTED in the service's registry
key, and QueryServiceConfig2 (A and W) returns them, laid out as Windows
does.  The failure actions are applied: when a service's process ends
without the service stopping (or, with the flag, when it stops reporting
an error) the action for the failure count -- restart, run a command with
%1% as the count, or nothing -- runs after its delay, the count restarting
once the reset period has passed.  No protocol change; the svcctl RPC
interface gains the launch-protected case and a reply header.

